# libGimbal allocates per-type class/type-info chunks in this function.
# Its process-exit type-registry finalizer destroys the metaclass registry without
# releasing every still-registered type's class chunk first. That shutdown leak
# belongs to the unmodified dependency, not libGumball-owned runtime state.
leak:GblType_updateTypeInfoClassChunk_

# Pinned libGimbal's deprecated GblTestScenario allocation tracker can leave the
# final instance allocations alive after reporting an unknown free during the
# objectBridge teardown path. The bridge objects reach cleanup with balanced
# references; ASan/UBSan and all unsuppressed leaks remain blocking.
leak:GUM_HierarchyTestSuite_objectBridge_
